==Battleground==
*9 [[Those Guys]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*6 [[Croco]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Kory]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
**6 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
**3 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Take advantage of the weak peons at the start and stall them with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]]/[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] for cash. After you hit the base, Kory appears alongside a total of 3 Shy Boys. If you have [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], bring it to shield against Kory's [[Wave Attack|Waves]]. The Shy Boys have a good amount of health so the use of [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] and [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] units is recommended. Possible options include [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]], and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]]. Lastly, be careful of the Ginger Snaches as a stack of them can easily tear through your weaker units.

==Trivia==
*This stage's Japanese name, The Fourth is Food!?, refers to [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]], who can also be obtained from the [[What's in the Box (Event Gacha)|What's in the Box]] gacha in [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]]. It was omitted from [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] because it already has the anniversary stage [[Faster Than Fast Food|Minced Meet-Up]] as a way to obtain Catburger.

